./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:3:A shared platform-contracts crate defines external principals, capability grants, action risk, approvals, audit envelopes, trace bundles, connected accounts, computer sessions, and exclusive control leases. Nine conflict-free worker streams build Meta-Harness, channel families, ACP, plugins, Composio, CUA, and teaching against that boundary while an integration owner alone edits central daemon, protocol, state, and application mounting surfaces. Meta-Harness diagnoses harness-caused failures from complete execution traces, proposes bounded shadow candidates, ranks them on a Pareto frontier, and promotes only through the existing signed self-evolution, canary, observation, and reversal path. Channel adapters normalize every platform through the durable gateway. ACP remains a client-to-agent protocol while MCP and plugins remain agent-to-tool protocols. Keith Computer is an isolated Linux workstation with semantic and visual observation, authenticated screen streaming, exclusive user-or-Keith input control, and a demonstration recorder that compiles synchronized screen, input, DOM, accessibility, and narration evidence into editable replayable TaskRecipes.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:9:Keith Everywhere is one expansion of the existing Keith product, not five adjacent products. The same daemon, profile, credentials, durable sessions, action inbox, approvals, audit records, event stream, resource governor, and client connection remain authoritative while five new capabilities are added:
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:14:4. Typed WASI plugins and Composio sessions connect external applications under Keith authority.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:17:The release succeeds only when these capabilities work together in one durable user journey.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:33:| 7 | Plugin ABI and host | Owns plugin SDK and host in dependency order |
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:34:| 8 | Composio and Apps | Owns connector crate and isolated Apps components |
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:35:| 9 | CUA runtime and co-control | Owns CUA crate, runner, and isolated ComputerStage components |
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:36:| 10 | Demonstrations and recipes | Owns task-recipe crate and isolated teaching components |
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:38:Only Agent 1 mounts isolated UI components into KeithApp, registers shared persisted collections, changes central protocol enums, or resolves cross-stream API differences. New crates are discovered by the workspace wildcard and do not require parallel edits to the root manifest.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:46:- ExternalPrincipal identifies the authenticated human, service account, channel sender, ACP client, plugin publisher, connector user, or computer observer.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:53:- CapabilityGrant names the allowed operation and bounded resource or target scope.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:74:4. A harness diagnosis names one causal component, reproduction, target metric, baseline, threshold, cost ceiling, and revert threshold.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:99:### 5.2 Capabilities
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:109:- Teams and Google Chat support their platform event, conversation, thread, mention, file, and card capabilities.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:111:- Matrix supports sync cursors, rooms, threads, replies, edits, reactions, media, reconnect, and an explicit encryption capability state.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:121:Client-provided filesystem, terminal, permission, and MCP capabilities become scoped tools. They cannot expand the profile workspace, credential, process, or network boundary. Stdio is the mandatory local transport; authenticated HTTP or SSE and WebSocket provide managed deployment. Draft v2 has separate handlers and feature gates with no silent conversion or downgrade.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:123:## 7. Plugin architecture
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:125:The existing plugin manifest and lifecycle become a typed WASI component platform.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:136:The plugin never receives an ambient directory, network, environment, process, or credential namespace. Manifests describe publisher, digest, signature, API compatibility, hooks, tools, schemas, grants, limits, and migration. Installation and update verify publisher continuity and show grant changes before approval. Quarantine and safe mode protect daemon startup.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:177:- Channels manages accounts, capabilities, routes, health, tests, pause, and removal.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:179:- Plugins manages packages, publishers, versions, grants, tools, health, updates, rollback, and uninstall.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:192:- Plugin invocations resolve to completed, cancelled, failed, or interrupted.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:203:External channel content, ACP clients, plugins, MCP servers, Composio results, websites, computer applications, recordings, recipes, traces, and candidate patches are mutually untrusted.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:205:No input from one surface can approve another surface, widen a grant, select another profile, expose a credential, install a plugin, connect an account, acquire computer control, enable self-evolution, alter an evaluator, or promote a candidate.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:211:- WASI traversal, resource exhaustion, network and credential escape.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:213:- SSRF and local-network access through tools, plugins, connectors, or computer navigation.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:237:- First channel round trips, ACP session, typed plugin invocation, Composio discovery, live computer action, and demonstration record work.
./spec/keith-everywhere/design.md:241:- Complete channel breadth, ACP capabilities and transports, plugin lifecycle, Apps UI, screen co-control, recipe replay, and harness promotion integration.
