./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:5:Keith Everywhere turns the existing persistent Keith runtime into one agent that can repair defects in its own harness through evidence, meet users across major communication channels, operate as an Agent Client Protocol agent, connect safely to external applications through plugins and Composio, and drive an isolated computer that users can watch, take over, and teach through demonstration. The program reuses the existing channel gateway, MCP manager, WASI plugin host, browser runner, self-evolution pipeline, daemon, sessions, profiles, credentials, and web client. Every surface shares explicit identity, permission, approval, audit, trace, cancellation, and recovery contracts. The ten-agent execution plan is encoded as conflict-aware dependency waves and no feature counts as complete without a real integrated journey.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:14:2. EVERY external action SHALL carry profile, session, acting principal, requested capability, action risk, approval state, cancellation identity, reply route where applicable, and audit correlation.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:15:3. THE most restrictive profile, session, connector, channel, ACP client, plugin, computer, and task policy SHALL win, and no adapter SHALL widen authority during translation.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:19:7. A contract suite SHALL prove serialization, version negotiation, denial on unknown capabilities, cancellation propagation, profile isolation, approval non-bypass, redaction, and exclusive control.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:27:1. CHANNEL adapters, ACP connections, plugin invocations, Composio sessions, computer sessions, recordings, recipes, and harness experiments SHALL have durable states with validated transitions.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:43:4. A proposed diagnosis SHALL name the causal harness component, reproduction, expected behavioral change, target metric, baseline, threshold, cost ceiling, and revert threshold before any edit.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:79:1. THE contract SHALL cover inbound events, outbound sends, identities, conversations, threads, replies, mentions, commands, edits, deletion, reactions, attachments, voice, rich content, typing, receipts, rate limits, reconnect, cancellation, and capability discovery.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:80:2. PLATFORM limitations SHALL be declared through capabilities and SHALL never be represented as successful unsupported behavior.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:118:1. KEITH SHALL implement stable ACP v1 initialization, capability negotiation, authentication metadata, session create, load, resume, fork, prompt, cancel, and terminal closure.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:125:## Requirement 10: ACP client capabilities, permissions, MCP, transports, and version boundary
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:131:1. CLIENT filesystem, terminal, permission, and MCP capabilities SHALL be represented as scoped tools and SHALL never widen the profile workspace, process, network, or credential boundary.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:138:## Requirement 11: Typed executable plugin ABI
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:140:**User Story:** As a plugin developer, I want real typed invocation rather than lifecycle-only hooks, so that extensions can safely add useful capabilities.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:144:1. THE plugin ABI SHALL carry versioned typed request and response payloads for command, tool, health, activation, migration, and deactivation.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:145:2. PLUGIN tools and commands SHALL register name, description, input and output schema, risk, timeout, cancellation, streaming, concurrency, and required grants.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:146:3. WASI components SHALL receive only explicit host calls for bounded HTTP, profile-local storage, named credentials, event emission, artifacts, clock, and safe logging.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:148:5. PACKAGE identity SHALL include manifest version, plugin id, version, API range, publisher, digest, signature, grants, hooks, tools, and migration contract.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:149:6. A conformance suite SHALL prove payload exchange, schema validation, cancellation, output streaming, grant denial, resource exhaustion, crash isolation, and secret redaction using real WASI components.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:151:## Requirement 12: Plugin lifecycle, provenance, catalog, and safe mode
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:153:**User Story:** As the owner, I want plugins to remain removable and auditable, so that extensibility cannot wedge or silently own Keith.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:159:3. NEW or widened grants SHALL require explicit human approval and SHALL NOT be inferred from plugin output or previous unrelated grants.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:160:4. SAFE mode SHALL start Keith with all third-party plugins disabled and SHALL remain available after a corrupt package, failed migration, crash loop, or incompatible API.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:161:5. THE web client SHALL present plugin identity, publisher, version, health, tools, grants, data access, recent calls, update diff, disable, rollback, and uninstall.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:231:**User Story:** As a user, I want these capabilities presented as one Keith rather than separate dashboards, so that control stays understandable.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:236:2. THE web app SHALL provide Channels, Apps, Plugins, ACP connections, Computers, Recordings, Recipes, and Harness Repairs without duplicating daemon business logic.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:248:1. CHANNEL content, ACP clients, plugins, Composio tools, websites, computer applications, recordings, recipes, traces, and candidate patches SHALL be treated as mutually untrusted inputs.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:249:2. AN input from one surface SHALL NOT enable self-evolution, install a plugin, connect an account, widen a grant, take computer control, approve an action, expose a credential, or select another profile.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:250:3. EXPORT and deletion SHALL cover channel accounts and events, ACP metadata, plugins, connected accounts, computer state, recordings, recipes, traces, candidates, and derived indexes with exact remnant reporting.
./spec/keith-everywhere/requirements.md:253:6. AN adversarial suite SHALL cover injection, SSRF, webhook forgery, protocol confusion, plugin escape, OAuth substitution, stream hijack, stale input, recording leakage, evaluator tampering, cross-profile access, and crash at every durable boundary.
./spec/keith-agent/design.body.md:7:Most assistants are still request-response applications. A message enters, a model produces text, tools may run, and the process eventually stops. Even when such a system has memory or scheduling, those capabilities are often attached as independent features rather than composed into one durable operating model.
./spec/keith-agent/design.body.md:43:**The Host-Authority Failure.** Shells, kernels, plugins, and browsers inherit the daemon user's complete filesystem, environment, and credentials.
./spec/keith-agent/design.body.md:97:All owned daemons, workers, protocols, providers, storage logic, clients, channels, memory services, schedulers, plugin hosts, and execution brokers are Rust. External interpreters are guests controlled through typed protocols and restricted process boundaries.
