- when the user later asked for "a handoff to start anew session" and wanted the handoff to focus on remaining work, stop promptly and leave a concise restart note centered on what is unfinished [Task 2][Task 3]

## Reusable knowledge

- `cortex.AppendMessage` is the durable session transcript store, and `cortex/provenance.go` resolves memory URIs back to exact transcript slices via `derived_from` provenance edges [Task 2]
- The lexical transcript lane is derived-only, wired through the vault seam, and must rebuild deterministically without altering `OverallRoot` [Task 2]
- `neo/internal/memory/pager.go` gained a hybrid reactive recall path where `Recall` can fall back to the lexical lane so `memory_recall` gets exact-word matching [Task 2]
- `neo/internal/server/episodic_sweep.go` plus `chronos/internal/episodicsweep` define a recurring idle backfill trigger with busy deferral rather than a user-facing turn [Task 2]
- Cassandra’s `trigEpisodicUngrounded` path and the client `memory.activation` / `buildTaskFromTrace` surface were part of the same DEJA-VU continuation, so future follow-up work in this family spans Cortex, Neo server, agent logic, and client traces together [Task 2]
- For DEJA-VU interruption recovery, the most reusable restart order is: recall file first, current spec status second, exact unfinished surface third, verification commands last [Task 3]
- A good restart note should name the exact remaining wave/task and the first validation checks, such as `jq` for locale files, `gofmt`, targeted Vitest/typecheck, then full build/vet/test and `spec/specgen` [Task 3]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: waves 2-4 look mostly implemented but the feature is not actually closed out. Cause: wave 4.3 client validation and wave 5 remained unfinished. Fix: separate "implemented" from "validated" and call out the exact remaining wave/task in the handoff [Task 2][Task 3]
- Symptom: large-file exploration gets truncated and patches become low-confidence. Cause: the files are too large for one-pass reads. Fix: inspect large files in smaller slices and verify exact file-level impacts before patching [Task 2]
- Symptom: a session turns into a restart request but work keeps expanding. Cause: scope did not stop when the user changed the goal. Fix: stop and hand off rather than continuing to widen the DEJA-VU scope [Task 2]

