acceptance criteria to satisfy:
  - THE plugin ABI SHALL carry versioned typed request and response payloads for command, tool, health, activation, migration, and deactivation.
  - PLUGIN tools and commands SHALL register name, description, input and output schema, risk, timeout, cancellation, streaming, concurrency, and required grants.
  - WASI components SHALL receive only explicit host calls for bounded HTTP, profile-local storage, named credentials, event emission, artifacts, clock, and safe logging.
  - INVOCATION SHALL enforce memory, fuel, input, output, time, process, filesystem, network, credential, and concurrent-call limits.
  - PACKAGE identity SHALL include manifest version, plugin id, version, API range, publisher, digest, signature, grants, hooks, tools, and migration contract.
  - A conformance suite SHALL prove payload exchange, schema validation, cancellation, output streaming, grant denial, resource exhaustion, crash isolation, and secret redaction using real WASI components.

